# .percolate-ignore — bin/ contributing source root for the claude-klabauter
# OSS mirror (row 4, `claude-klabauter-bin`, authored sibling-side in
# DoE-claude:setup/publish-targets.portable).
#
# SOURCE_DIR for this file is `claude-klabauter/bin/` itself. Patterns are
# SOURCE_DIR-RELATIVE — they carry NO `bin/` prefix, or they double-prefix to
# `bin/bin/…` and match nothing. Same trap the sibling
# `coordinator_core/.percolate-ignore` header warns about; read that file's
# MECHANISM block for the full single-source explanation, which applies here
# verbatim (row 4 is likewise single-source, so this file is inert during
# restricted-tree assembly and becomes live only when `dispatch_mirror_like`
# hands it to `sync_mirror`, which consults it symmetrically on both the copy
# and destination-delete legs).
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: row 4's allowlist admits `tests`, and the first
# resolved dry-run against the live destination (2026-08-02) put 27
# `__pycache__/*.pyc` files into the publish set — build artifacts from two
# interpreter versions, carrying no source value and pinning local pytest
# versions into a public artifact. The allowlist cannot express this: it gates
# top-level entries, and `__pycache__` appears nested under an admitted one.
#
# The published test suite itself SHIPS and must keep shipping — same PM
# ruling as row 1 (§ C3, "settled, do not re-argue"): the tests are the
# adopter's means of verifying an install. Do NOT add `tests/` here.

# --- Python build artifacts ---
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/

# --- Editor / OS detritus ---
*.bak
*.tmp
*.swp
*.swo
*~
*.orig
*.rej
# Bare (unprefixed) names match ONLY at this file's own root (exact full
# rel_path match); a `*`-leading basename glob is required to also catch these
# nested inside bin/'s subdirectories.
*.DS_Store
*Thumbs.db
*desktop.ini
